r.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivangorod"><span class="enc-name">Ivangorod</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivangorod is a town in Leningrad Oblast, Russia, on the Narva River opposite the Estonian city of Narva.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivanko-of-dobruja"><span class="enc-name">Ivanko of Dobruja</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivanko was the son of Dobrotitsa and the last ruler of the Dobrujan principality on the Black Sea, from about 1386.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivano-frankivsk"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ivano-frankivsk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ivano-Frankivsk</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivano-Frankivsk is a city in western Ukraine at the foot of the Carpathians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivar-of-limerick"><span class="enc-name">Ivar of Limerick</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivar of Limerick was the Norse king of Limerick in the later 10th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/iverni"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/iverni.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Iverni</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Iverni were a people of southern Ireland recorded in Ptolemy's Geography of about 150 CE, with a town called Ivernis in the region of modern Cork or Kerry.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/iviron-monastery"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/iviron-monastery.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Iviron Monastery</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Iviron Monastery is an Eastern